# koi-network-allow.default — hosts the sandbox may reach without asking.
#
# Sibling of sandbox-exclude.default, same deal: this is DEPLOYMENT policy, not
# server policy. The installer seeds ~/.koi/network-policy.json from this file
# the first time it runs and never touches it again — after that the file the
# user (or the approval dialog) edits is the JSON, not this one.
#
# Format: one host pattern per line. `#` comments and blank lines ignored.
#   example.com          exact host
#   *.example.com        host and any subdomain
#   example.com:443      narrow to specific ports (comma-separated)
#   !example.com         explicit DENY — always wins over any allow, including
#                        a later approval dialog
#   192.0.2.10           a bare IP is just another host string
#
# IP addresses are matched EXACTLY and do not inherit a name's grant: allowing
# `github.com` does not allow the address it resolves to, because a CDN can
# move that address to someone else. Approve an IP only if you mean that IP.
#
# CIDR ranges are NOT supported. `10.0.0.0/8` is compared as a literal string
# and therefore matches nothing — list each address you need on its own line.
#
# Everything not matched here falls through to the policy's `default`, which is
# "ask": the request is held and the side panel prompts. In an unattended run
# (TopicRunner worker, --full-auto) there is nobody to ask, so it is denied.
#
# In a locked-down corporate environment, empty this file and add only your
# internal mirrors.

# --- source hosting ---
github.com
*.github.com
codeload.github.com
raw.githubusercontent.com
objects.githubusercontent.com
gitlab.com
*.gitlab.com
bitbucket.org

# --- node ---
registry.npmjs.org
*.npmjs.org
registry.yarnpkg.com

# --- python ---
pypi.org
files.pythonhosted.org
*.pythonhosted.org

# --- rust ---
crates.io
static.crates.io
index.crates.io

# --- go ---
proxy.golang.org
sum.golang.org

# --- distro packages (build deps inside the overlay) ---
archive.ubuntu.com
security.ubuntu.com
deb.debian.org

# --- explicit denials -------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud instance metadata: a read of this endpoint is a credential theft, and
# it is reachable from anything running on a cloud dev box.
!169.254.169.254
!metadata.google.internal
